      body: ["Recorded with Max Martin and Shellback, it was relegated to the deluxe edition in 2014, then finally released as 1989's seventh and last single in February 2016 — with a Jonas Åkerlund video stitched from 1989 World Tour footage that premiered exclusively on Apple Music.", "No. 58 among the 100 best songs of the 2010s on Rolling Stone's 2019 decade-end list — \"the type of relieving dance floor soul purge that the best pop can be,\" and by the writer's own argument, the bonus track was the album's real thesis: a heartbroken hopeless romantic finding power in the pain. Critics keep ranking it among her best songs, usually with the same complaint attached: it never made the standard tracklist."],
