      date: "2007-12-22",
      dateLabel: "December 22, 2007",
      title: "Our Song becomes her first No. 1",
      summary: "Six weeks atop Hot Country Songs — the first of what would become seven country No. 1s before her pivot to pop.",
      body: ["In December 2007 it began a six-week reign at No. 1 on Hot Country Songs — a song she had written alone for her ninth-grade talent show, which made her, per Wikipedia's chart accounting, the youngest person ever to single-handedly write and sing a Hot Country Songs No. 1.", "Its jump to the top from No. 6 was the chart's biggest leap since 1998. She never claimed to have seen it coming: \"I never thought it was going to be on an album... I never thought it would be a single, I never thought it would go No. 1.\""],
