      body: ["Taylor and Lively co-wrote the video's concept, and the song itself carries Chris Stapleton's harmonies — the twangiest thing in the entire vault.", "The casting kept it in the family: Miles Teller's bride is played by his real-life wife, Keleigh Sperry, and Taylor's own announcement framed the collaboration as overdue — \"I finally got to work with the brilliant, brave, & wickedly funny @blakelively on her directorial debut. Join us as we raise a toast, and a little hell.\" It was the friends' first official creative project together, years after Taylor borrowed the names of Lively and Ryan Reynolds' daughters for folklore's \"betty.\""],
