      date: "2019-08-23",
      dateLabel: "August 23, 2019",
      title: "Miss Americana & the Heartbreak Prince, a high school built from 2018's political disillusionment",
      summary: "Written with Joel Little after the midterms: \"This song is about disillusionment with our crazy world of politics and inequality, set in a metaphorical high school.\"",
      body: ["In her Spotify storyline, Taylor said: \"This song is about disillusionment with our crazy world of politics and inequality, set in a metaphorical high school... I wanted it to be about finding one person who really sees you and cares about you through all the noise.\"", "She expanded on it to Rolling Stone: \"It's about the illusions of what I thought America was before our political landscape took this turn, and that naivete that we used to have about it,\" written \"a couple of months after midterm elections.\""],
