      id: "vault-midnights-1989-taylors-version-announced-at-the-final-us-show-on-the-d",
      slug: "sofi-1989-tv-announcement",
      date: "2023-08-09",
      dateLabel: "August 9, 2023",
      title: "1989 (Taylor's Version) announced at the final US show — on the date fans predicted",
      summary: "Blue versions of her Speak Now, folklore, and 1989 outfits teased it all night at SoFi before the reveal: Oct. 27. Fans had already done the math — Aug. 9 was eight years, nine months, and 13 days since the original.",
      body: ["The Aug. 9, 2023 finale of the tour's first US run landed the reveal in the acoustic surprise-song slot: the new album cover — Taylor smiling against a blue sky, echoing the 2014 original — flashed onto the stadium screens to a roughly eight-minute roar, and she paired the night with \"New Romantics\" on guitar and \"New Year's Day\" on piano. She called it \"my most FAVORITE re-record I've ever done because the 5 From The Vault tracks are so insane.\"", "The date numerology (8/9 reading as '89, and her lucky 13) had circulated among fans for weeks — one of the rare times the fandom called an announcement to the day, with the era's blue color-code and the tour calendar all pointing the same way before the show.", "The five vault-track titles came via a September Google puzzle hunt — fans were set 33 million word-scrambles to solve (a nod to her age) and blew past it in a day, crashing the counter. All five landed in the Hot 100's top 10 at release: \"Is It Over Now?\" debuted at No. 1 (her second Taylor's Version vault cut to top the chart, after \"All Too Well\"), trailed by \"Now That We Don't Talk,\" \"Slut!,\" \"Say Don't Go\" and \"Suburban Legends\" — and 1989 (Taylor's Version) opened to the biggest week of her career."],
      tags: ["Music"],
      images: [{ url: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Taylor_Swift_The_Eras_Tour_Midnights_Era_Set_%2853109617451%29.jpg/960px-Taylor_Swift_The_Eras_Tour_Midnights_Era_Set_%2853109617451%29.jpg", credit: "Paolo V, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons", caption: "The Midnights set at SoFi Stadium on Aug. 9, 2023 — the final US show of the year, and the night the 1989 (Taylor's Version) announcement lit up the roof.", kind: "primary", focalPoint: "48% 30%" }, { url: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/de/Taylor_Swift_The_Eras_Tour_1989_Era_Set_%2853109523971%29_%28cropped%29.jpg", credit: "Paolo V, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons", caption: "Taylor in the blue-crystal 1989 era set at SoFi Stadium that night — the color-coded tease that fans read as a signal before the 1989 (Taylor's Version) reveal.", kind: "primary", focalPoint: "51% 15%" }],
      sources: [{ name: "Taylor Swift Says '1989 (Taylor's Version)' Is Coming at L.A. Finale", url: "https://variety.com/2023/music/news/taylor-swift-announces-1989-taylors-version-coming-la-tour-finale-sofi-stadium-1235692622/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Taylor Swift announces '1989 (Taylor's Version)' at final U.S. Eras Tour show this year", url: "https://www.washingtonpost.com/arts-entertainment/2023/08/10/taylor-swift-1989-taylors-version/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "1989 (Taylor's Version)", url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1989_(Taylor%27s_Version)", reliability: 2, type: "wiki" }, { name: "Taylor Swift Eras Tour LA Night 6 Recap: Best Moments at SoFi Stadium", url: "https://www.billboard.com/lists/taylor-swift-eras-tour-la-recap-night-6-best-moments-sofi-stadium/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Taylor Swift Fans Crash Google Solving 1989 Vault Puzzles", url: "https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-fans-crash-google-1989-vault-puzzles-1235416529/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Taylor Swift's 'Is It Over Now?' Debuts at No. 1 on the Hot 100", url: "https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/taylor-swift-is-it-over-now-number-1-hot-100-debut-1235464462/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "1989 (Taylor's Version) Gives Taylor Swift Her Best First Week Ever", url: "https://variety.com/2023/music/news/taylor-swift-number-one-1989-taylors-version-her-best-first-week-ever-1235780769/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }],
      milestone: { id: "m-mid-6", label: "1989 (TV) announced", kind: "album" },
