      id: "vault-ttpd-the-tortured-poets-department",
      slug: "ttpd-album",
      date: "2024-04-19",
      dateLabel: "April 19, 2024",
      title: "The Tortured Poets Department",
      summary: "A literary, ink-stained double album — the most word-heavy record of her career.",
      body: ["Announced from the Grammy stage on Feb. 4, 2024 — she revealed the April 19 release date while accepting Best Pop Vocal Album for Midnights and unveiled the cover on the podium — TTPD arrived as a surprise double album. Sixteen standard tracks dropped at midnight ET; two hours later, at 2 a.m. ET, fifteen more appeared as \"The Tortured Poets Department: The Anthology,\" 31 songs in all.", "Jack Antonoff and Aaron Dessner produced it alongside Taylor — the two collaborators who defined the folklore-through-Midnights run — splitting the work almost by half: Antonoff led the standard sixteen tracks, Dessner the fifteen-song Anthology, whose hushed folk cuts (\"How Did It End?,\" \"The Albatross,\" \"The Black Dog\") are largely his. It carries two features: Post Malone on the lead single \"Fortnight\" and Florence + the Machine on \"Florida!!!.\" Four collectible deluxe editions each carried a different bonus track — \"The Manuscript,\" \"The Bolter,\" \"The Albatross\" and \"The Black Dog\" — before all four were folded into the Anthology.", "The title is widely linked to a \"Tortured Man Club\" group chat Joe Alwyn shared with actors Paul Mescal and Andrew Scott (Alwyn confirmed the chat in a 2022 interview; Taylor has never named it as the source). It opened to 2.61 million first-week units in the U.S. — her 14th No. 1 on the Billboard 200, tying Jay-Z for the most chart-toppers among soloists — and was Spotify's most-streamed album in a single day. Reviews were admiring but split (Metacritic 76): critics praised the cathartic writing while calling the 31-track sprawl overlong.", "It set records well past the first week: the first album in Spotify history to pass one billion streams in a single week, after also taking the single-day album and single-day song (\"Fortnight\") records on April 19 — and it monopolized all top 14 of the Billboard Hot 100, a first for any artist. Live, the album reshaped the Eras Tour: the May 9, 2024 European opener at Paris La Défense Arena debuted a new act Taylor nicknamed \"Female Rage: The Musical,\" folding in seven TTPD songs — among them \"Fortnight,\" \"But Daddy I Love Him,\" \"Down Bad,\" \"So High School\" and \"I Can Do It With a Broken Heart\" — and trimming older cuts to fit. Beyond that scripted act, TTPD tracks worked their way into the acoustic surprise slot through 2024 — \"Paris\" and \"loml\" were the first, at the Paris opener — and she held \"So Long, London\" back until the final Wembley night, debuting it solo on piano. Awards ran hot then cold: \"Fortnight\" won Video of the Year and Best Collaboration in a seven-VMA night in 2024, but at the 67th Grammys (Feb. 2, 2025) TTPD drew Taylor a record seventh Album of the Year nomination and a Best Pop Vocal Album nod and won neither — AOTY went to Beyoncé's Cowboy Carter, Best Pop Vocal Album to Sabrina Carpenter."],
      tags: ["Music"],
      images: [{ url: "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/RQMz4JDbtmI/maxresdefault.jpg", credit: "Taylor Swift / Republic Records (official title-track lyric video, YouTube)", caption: "The album’s monochrome “department” visual, from the official title-track lyric video.", kind: "primary", focalPoint: "50% 48%" }, { url: "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4wOsiM2T_xc/maxresdefault.jpg", credit: "Taylor Swift / Republic Records (official “The Albatross” lyric video, YouTube)", caption: "The black-and-gray title card from the official “The Albatross” lyric video.", kind: "primary", focalPoint: "50% 50%" }],
      sources: [{ name: "Taylor Swift Shares Tracklist for 'The Tortured Poets Department,' Featuring Post Malone and Florence + Machine", url: "https://variety.com/2024/music/news/taylor-swift-tracklist-the-tortured-poets-department-post-malone-florence-machine-1235898976/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Taylor Swift's 'The Tortured Poets Department' Debuts at No. 1 on Billboard 200 With 2.61 Million Units", url: "https://www.billboard.com/lists/taylor-swift-tortured-poets-department-debut-number-one-billboard-200-chart/", reliability: 4, type: "awards_database" }, { name: "Taylor Swift Sets Record With All Top 14 of Hot 100, 'Fortnight' No. 1", url: "https://www.billboard.com/lists/taylor-swift-hot-100-top-14-fortnight-post-malone-record/", reliability: 4, type: "awards_database" }, { name: "The Tortured Poets Department by Taylor Swift Reviews", url: "https://www.metacritic.com/music/the-tortured-poets-department/taylor-swift", reliability: 3, type: "aggregator" }, { name: "Joe Alwyn's Tortured Man Club Group Chat Explained", url: "https://www.newsweek.com/entertainment-celebrity-news-joe-alwyn-tortured-man-club-group-chat-explained-andrew-scott-1903714", reliability: 3, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "THE TORTURED POETS DEPARTMENT Becomes the First Album to Surpass One Billion Streams in a Single Week on Spotify", url: "https://newsroom.spotify.com/2024-04-24/tortured-poets-department-taylor-swift-one-billion-record-streams/", reliability: 5, type: "official" }, { name: "How Taylor Swift's 'Tortured Poets Department' changes the 'Eras Tour'", url: "https://www.today.com/popculture/music/eras-tour-tortured-poets-department-set-list-rcna151509", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Taylor Swift Wins Video of the Year for 'Fortnight' at 2024 VMAs", url: "https://www.billboard.com/music/awards/taylor-swift-wins-video-of-the-year-fortnight-vmas-2024-1235773569/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Beyoncé's 'Cowboy Carter' Wins Album Of The Year At The 2025 Grammys", url: "https://www.forbes.com/sites/monicamercuri/2025/02/03/beyoncs-cowboy-carter-wins-album-of-the-year-at-the-2025-grammys/", reliability: 4, type: "reputable_press" }, { name: "Taylor Swift's 'The Tortured Poets Department': here are the full album credits", url: "https://www.nme.com/news/music/taylor-swifts-the-tortured-poets-department-here-are-the-full-album-credits-3619931", reliability: 3, type: "reputable_press" }],
      hiddenClue: { clue: "A second half — “The Anthology” — appeared two hours after release.", payoff: "The surprise 15 extra tracks doubled the album and broke streaming records overnight." },
